#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
pchome - agent-native CLI for PChome 24h購物 (24h.pchome.com.tw, TWD). No checkout.

Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib). Every command supports --json and
returns the {ok, data|error} envelope used by the other ~/Projects CLIs.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 api, 2 usage, 3 auth, 4 net/blocked.

Endpoints, measured 2026-10-29 with real requests (plain HTTPS + browser UA
works for all of them; none was bot-walled):

  search   GET ecshweb.pchome.com.tw/search/v4.3/all/results
             ?q=..&page=N&sort=rnk/dc|sale/dc|prc/ac|prc/dc|new/dc&price=MIN-MAX
           -> {TotalRows, TotalPage, Prods:[{Id, Name, Describe, Price,
               OriginPrice, ratingValue, reviewCount, isPChome, ...}]}  20/page
  product  GET ecapi-cdn.pchome.com.tw/ecshop/prodapi/v2/prod/<ID>&fields=...
             (or prod?id=A,B&fields=... for many). The path-style URLs
             (prod/<ID>&.., prod/spec&id=.., /desc) answer an EMPTY 200 unless
             `&_callback=<name>` is added (JSONP); the CLI always adds it -> {<ID>-000: {Name, Price:{M,P,Prime,Low}, Qty,
             isSpec, Store, ShipType, isArrival24h, PreOrdDate, ...}}
           GET .../prodapi/v2/prod/spec&id=<ID>   specs (尺寸/顏色) with ids
             <ID>-003.. and stock Qty
           GET .../prodapi/v2/prod/button&id=A,B&fields=Id,Price,Qty,ButtonType,
             SaleStatus   price/stock/buyability per spec id (price check)
           GET .../prodapi/v2/prod/<ID>/desc&fields=Slogan,...  promo blurb
  member   GET ecapi.pchome.com.tw/member/v2/member/islogin   -> 1 / 0
           GET ecapi.pchome.com.tw/member/v2/member  -> {LoginEmail (masked),
             LoginMobile (masked), PCoin, CashPoint} or {Code:403}
           GET ecapi.pchome.com.tw/member/v2/member/id -> "full@email" or null
  cart     GET ecssl.pchome.com.tw/sys/cflow/fsapi/BigCar/BIGCAR/ItemList
             -> itemlist.houses.<24H|ITEM_0_ALL..>.packages[].items{Key:{IT_SNO,
                SR_NO, IT_NAME, QTY, PRICE, SPEC, StockQTY, ...}}, totalPrice
           GET ecssl-cart.pchome.com.tw/sys/cflow/ecapi/prod/cart/v1/prod/<ID>/snapup
             -> {MAC, MACExpire} (anti-bot token, ~15 min) needed by ADD
           GET ecssl-cart.pchome.com.tw/cart/index.php/prod/modify?callback=..&data=
             {"G":[],"A":[],"B":[],"C":[],"TB":"24H","TP":2,"T":"ADD",
              "TI":"<ID>-000","RS":"<Store>","YTQ":qty,"CAX":MAC,"CAXE":MACExpire}
             -> JSONP {PRODTOTAL, PRODCOUNT, ...}   (also the web app's add button)
           POST ecssl.pchome.com.tw/sys/cflow/fsapi/BigCar/BIGCAR/modifyItem
             form data={"T":"DEL","TI","RS","TTI":"A","KEY","LB":"Y"}   remove
             form data={"T":"UPD","TI","YTQ","RS","TB":"24H","KEY","LB":"Y"} qty
             -> empty 200; the CLI re-reads ItemList to confirm.
  The cart is tied to the ECWEBSESS cookie (works for a guest too; a guest
  cart is merged into the member cart on sign-in). Everything under
  /sys/cflow other than the four calls above (checkout, orders, payment) is
  never called.

Login: PChome uses password + reCAPTCHA (+ OTP), so the CLI never handles
credentials. `pchome login` (default --from-browser) reads the pchome cookies
from the Edge/Chrome on CDP (PCHOME_CDP, default http://127.0.0.1:9222); if
that browser is not signed in it opens the login page in a BACKGROUND tab and
polls until you sign in there yourself (--wait, default 300 s), then closes
only that tab. Also --from-clipboard / --cookie-stdin. The cookie is verified
over plain HTTP (member/islogin + member/id) before it is saved to
~/.config/pchome/state.json (0600) or the OS keyring (--keyring).
PCHOME_COOKIE overrides both. Cart commands always use the SAVED session.

Transport: HTTP first; on a 403/HTML challenge the same GET is retried with
fetch() inside a background tab of the CDP browser (--via auto|http|browser).

Unofficial. Undocumented, private API - it can break without warning.
No checkout / payment / order placement, by design.
"""
